  "original_problem_statement": "# ParseError shows incorrect line number in error message\n\nWhen using the `ParseError` class, the line number shown in the error message is incorrect. It's showing the line number minus 1 instead of the line number plus 1.\n\n## To Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom iniconfig.exceptions import ParseError\n\n# Create a ParseError with line number 0\ne = ParseError('filename', 0, 'hello')\nprint(str(e))\n```\n\n### Current output:\n```\nfilename:-1: hello\n```\n\n### Expected output:\n```\nfilename:1: hello\n```\n\nThe issue is that the line number is being decremented instead of incremented when formatting the error message. This causes line numbers to be off by 2 from what they should be, and can even result in negative line numbers when the error is on the first line of a file.\n\nThis is particularly confusing for users trying to debug configuration issues, as they'll be looking at the wrong line in their files.",
